,"id":16980628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2OTgwNjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16980628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB","html_url":"https://github.com/LizzyTB","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LizzyTB/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-16T14:47:41Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T14:47:41Z","body":"When creating this PR, I was thinking that it could be used at runtime so that projects could implement a texture quality setting in a settings menu so that developers can target a wider range of hardware. I know as a quick hack, you could set the mipmap bias. The problem is that the full texture is still loaded into memory.\r\n\r\nMaybe a better solution would be to have the importer write multiple ctex files at different resolutions and then pick the appropriate one at runtime?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193716304/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193759311","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109650#issuecomment-3193759311","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109650","id":3193759311,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6-XOZP","user":{"login":"BlueCube3310","id":53150244,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMTUwMjQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53150244?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310","html_url":"https://github.com/BlueCube3310","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlueCube3310/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-16T16:07:53Z","updated_at":"2025-08-16T16:07:53Z","body":"> When creating this PR, I was thinking that it could be used at runtime so that projects could implement a texture quality setting in a settings menu so that developers can target a wider range of hardware. I know as a quick hack, you could set the mipmap bias. The problem is that the full texture is still loaded into memory.\r\n> \r\n> Maybe a better solution would be to have the importer write multiple ctex files at different resolutions and then pick the appropriate one at runtime?\r\n\r\nThe aforementioned feature doesn't just set the mipmap bias, it forces the file reader to skip to later parts of the data in the file, then treats the following mipmap as the base image (with a lower resolution than the actual image).\r\n\r\nFor proper runtime texture quality changes, a more robust solution such as texture streaming is necessary.\r\n\r\nHaving multiple .ctex files will take up a lot of space in exported projects. Having separate resolution settings per platform/export preset seems like an alternative solution: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10034","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3193759311/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]